senses.gloss:
Bakkula, Bakula, Vakkula, Vakula, Vatkula,
(1) (= Pali Bakkula, Bākula, Vakkula), n. of a disciple of Buddha: Bakkula SP 〔2.5〕; 〔207.4〕; Bakula (the same person?) Karmav 〔76.11〕, called king of Kashmir and son of Dharmayaśas, noted for his health and long life, which in Pali is a characteristic of the thera Ba˚; Vakkula LV 〔2.2〕 (v.l. Vakula; Tib. Ba ku la); Sukh 〔92.8〕; Mvy 〔1065〕 (var. Vakula; Tib. Ba ku la, or Bag ku la); Vakula Sukh 〔2.9〕; MSV 〔i.192.18 ff.〕; Vatkula Divy 〔396.2 f.〕;
(2) n. of two vakṣas: Māy 〔6, 54〕 (Lévi Vakula).
